-A visit is booked against a particular pet and carries the date it is for and a short description of what it is for `[REQ-VIS-001]`. When booking, the pet's earlier visits are shown alongside, so whoever is booking can see what has already been done `[REQ-VIS-002]`.
+A visit is booked against a particular pet and carries the date it is for and a short description of what it is for `[REQ-VIS-001]`. When booking, the pet's earlier visits are shown alongside, so whoever is booking can see what has already been done `[REQ-VIS-002]`. A booked visit's date and description can be corrected afterwards. A correction meets the same rules the booking met, and it replaces that visit rather than adding a second one `[REQ-VIS-003]`.
 
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a pet, when a description and a date later than today are supplied, then the visit is recorded and the booking is confirmed.
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a blank description, when the visit is submitted, then the booking is refused and the description is named.
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a date of today or earlier, when the visit is submitted, then the booking is refused and the date is named.
 - `[REQ-VIS-002]` given a pet with earlier visits, when a new visit is being booked, then those earlier visits are shown with their dates and descriptions.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a booked visit, when its correction is begun, then the visit's current date and description are offered for changing.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a booked visit, when a description and a date later than today are supplied, then that visit carries the new date and description.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a correction that is accepted, when it is stored, then no further visit is recorded and the owner's record is shown.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a blank description, when the correction is submitted, then the correction is refused, the description is named, and the visit is left as it was.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a date of today or earlier, when the correction is submitted, then the correction is refused, the date is named, and the visit is left as it was.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. Booking a visit for a pet that does not belong to the named owner is refused.
 2. The date offered by default is the earliest date that would be accepted.
+3. Correcting a visit is refused when the pet does not belong to the named owner, or when the visit does not belong to the named pet.
+4. A visit whose date has already passed can be corrected only by moving its date later than today, so its description cannot be corrected on its own.
+
+**ADR:** [ADR: Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope; Cancelling One Is Not](adr/2026-08-11-non-goal-visit-correction-narrowing.md)
 
